  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "A decorator's metadata object is not a fact any Pack emits, so selector, templateUrl, styleUrls, imports, providers, declarations and exports are unreadable. A component reaches its template by the sibling *.component.html the CLI generates beside it, and by nothing else.",
      "omega-html emits no per-attribute fact, so Angular's authored template syntax -- [input], (event), [(banana)], *ngIf, #ref, routerLink and the interpolations -- is outside the overlay entirely. What a template states is its custom elements.",
      "inject(Service) and @ViewChild(Child) carry their subject as a call argument, and no Pack publishes call argument text; the constructor-parameter spelling of injection is reachable because TypeScript writes the type as a type annotation.",
      "Router configuration is an array of object literals whose paths are string values; no Pack emits them, so which URL reaches which component is not stated.",
      "Runtime-generated views, injector hierarchy and provider selection, change detection and dynamic component creation require runtime evidence."
    ]
  },
